From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:44:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: sun60i_dp: Unwind the bridge attach on failure

sun60i_dp_bridge_attach() attaches the next bridge, then sets
aux.drm_dev and registers the AUX channel. If the registration fails,
the next bridge stays in the encoder's chain and aux.drm_dev still
points at a drm_device that the failed bind frees. The core removes
only this bridge from the chain and does not call .detach, and without
CONFIG_DRM_DISPLAY_DP_AUX_CHARDEV nothing clears the field; the AUX
helpers use it in their debug messages and warnings. In that
configuration .detach leaves the same stale field after an unbind.

Register the AUX channel first, as ti-sn65dsi86 does, then attach the
next bridge, and undo the steps in reverse order when one fails.
drm_dp_aux_register() warns if drm_dev is not set, so it has to be set
before the call and cleared again on failure. Clear it in .detach too.

Not covered: on success only the order changes, the AUX channel is now
registered before the next bridge attaches; the fault is not seen
without injecting an error.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: with the AUX registration and the next
bridge made to fail in turn, each failed attach cleared aux.drm_dev and
left no AUX adapter behind, and the next bind brought the picture back.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun60i_dp.c | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun60i_dp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun60i_dp.c
index 152ef573d4d0..c548d8032ad0 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun60i_dp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun60i_dp.c
@@ -978,13 +978,24 @@ static int sun60i_dp_bridge_attach(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 	if (!(flags & DRM_BRIDGE_ATTACH_NO_CONNECTOR))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	dp->aux.drm_dev = bridge->dev;
+
+	ret = drm_dp_aux_register(&dp->aux);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_drm_dev;
+
 	ret = drm_bridge_attach(encoder, dp->next_bridge, bridge, flags);
 	if (ret)
-		return ret;
+		goto err_aux;
 
-	dp->aux.drm_dev = bridge->dev;
+	return 0;
 
-	return drm_dp_aux_register(&dp->aux);
+err_aux:
+	drm_dp_aux_unregister(&dp->aux);
+err_drm_dev:
+	dp->aux.drm_dev = NULL;
+
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static void sun60i_dp_bridge_detach(struct drm_bridge *bridge)
@@ -992,6 +1003,7 @@ static void sun60i_dp_bridge_detach(struct drm_bridge *bridge)
 	struct sun60i_dp *dp = bridge_to_sun60i_dp(bridge);
 
 	drm_dp_aux_unregister(&dp->aux);
+	dp->aux.drm_dev = NULL;
 }
 
